/-
Copyright: subproject `OROneRel` -- one-relator combinatorics (node N2).

# The Nielsen route to the "no exponent sum zero" Magnus step

This file isolates a *conditional* but completely proved reduction of the target lemma
`Work.OROneRel.magnus_step_root_no_eps_zero` (see `Submission/Work/OROneRel/magnus_step_root_no_eps_zero.lean`)
to a purely combinatorial statement about Nielsen transformations of words.

## The step that is available

`Work.OROneRel.magnusStepCase2_of_weight` (proved in the workspace) states that, for a root `u` with
`¬ IsProperPower u`, cyclically reduced, `2 ≤ relatorNorm u` and all exponent sums non-zero, the
conclusion of the Magnus step holds as soon as there are a letter `t` and a weight `c : α → ℤ` with

* `t ∈ relatorLetters u`, `c t = 1` and `cohom c u = 1` (i.e. `Σ_x c_x * eps_x u = 0`).

The last condition is the **divisibility condition**: with `c t = 1` it is solvable for `c` exactly
when `gcd {eps_x u : x ≠ t}` divides `eps_t u`, so it says that some letter's exponent sum lies in
the ideal generated by the other letters' exponent sums.

## The reduction proved here

The step is applied to an *automorphic image* `ψ u` of `u`: an automorphism `ψ` of `F α` induces an
isomorphism `⟨α | u ^ l⟩ ≃* ⟨α | (ψ u) ^ l⟩` carrying the class of `u` to the class of `ψ u`
(`nielsenPowerIso`), so the HNN data for `⟨α | (ψ u) ^ l⟩` transports back to `u`
(`MagnusStepData.of_aut`).  Consequently the target follows from the single condition

  `∃ ψ : F α ≃* F α, relatorNorm (ψ u) ≤ relatorNorm u ∧ (ψ u satisfies the divisibility condition)`

(`magnusStepData_of_divisible_image`), because the step at `ψ u` produces a root of norm
`< relatorNorm (ψ u) ≤ relatorNorm u`.

## What this leaves open (recorded for the next session)

The remaining combinatorial question is whether every `u` (cyclically reduced, `¬ IsProperPower u`,
`relatorNorm u ≥ 2`, all exponent sums non-zero) has a Nielsen image `ψ u` with the divisibility
condition and `relatorNorm (ψ u) ≤ relatorNorm u`.

* If the divisibility already holds for `u` itself (e.g. whenever two distinct exponent sums are
  coprime, so for `a ^ 2 b ^ 3 c ^ 5`, or whenever some exponent sum is `±1` *and* the gcd of the
  others is `1`), no automorphism is needed: `magnusStepCase2_of_weight` applies outright.
* For the two-letter torus-knot-type roots `x ^ p y ^ q` (`p, q ≥ 2`, `gcd = 1`) the divisibility for
  `u` itself fails, but a *weight* step applied to an automorphic image succeeds whenever the image
  has few non-`t` letters; this is how `x ^ 2 y ^ 3`, `x ^ 3 y ^ 5`, `x ^ 5 y ^ 4` are reached.  For
  `x ^ 3 y ^ 8` (and `x ^ 4 y ^ 7`) the natural transvection family misses the bound by exactly one,
  and an exhaustive search over the Nielsen orbit up to word length `120` finds no witness; whether
  a witness exists at all in these cases is *open* here and is the precise content of the
  combinatorial condition above.

The companion lemma `magusStepData_of_aut_divisible` (sic) below is stated with the *raw* exponent
sum condition rather than a `gcd` condition, so that no arithmetic lemma is needed.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.Basic
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.MagnusRewrite
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.MagnusGenDefs
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.magnusStepCase2_of_weight
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.magnusStepCase2_of_weight_count

namespace Work.OROneRel

universe u

/-- **The conclusion of the Magnus step**, as a `Prop` (this is the conclusion of the target lemma
`Work.OROneRel.magnus_step_root_no_eps_zero`, kept under a distinct name so that this module can be
imported alongside `Submission.Work.OROneRel.magnus_step_root`, which declares the same shape under
the name `HasMagnusStepAt`). -/
abbrev MagnusStepData {α : Type u} (u : FreeGroup α) (l : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∃ (β : Type u) (v : FreeGroup β), ¬ IsProperPower v ∧ relatorNorm v < relatorNorm u ∧
    ∃ (A B : Subgroup (PresentedGroup ({v ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup β)))) (φ : A ≃* B)
      (e : PresentedGroup ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) ≃*
        HNNExtension (PresentedGroup ({v ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup β))) A B φ),
      ∃ c : HNNExtension (PresentedGroup ({v ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup β))) A B φ,
        e (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) u) =
          c * HNNExtension.of (PresentedGroup.mk ({v ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup β)) v) * c⁻¹

/-- **A Nielsen image gives an isomorphic root presentation.**  An automorphism `ψ` of `F α` maps the
normal closure of `u ^ l` onto the normal closure of `(ψ u) ^ l`, hence induces an isomorphism of the
one-relator presentations which carries the class of `u` to the class of `ψ u`. -/
theorem nielsenPowerIso {α : Type u} (ψ : FreeGroup α ≃* FreeGroup α) (u : FreeGroup α) (l : ℕ) :
    ∃ e : PresentedGroup ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) ≃*
        PresentedGroup ({(ψ u) ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)),
      e (PresentedGroup.mk ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) u) =
        PresentedGroup.mk ({(ψ u) ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) (ψ u) := by
  have hmap : Subgroup.map (↑ψ) (Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))
      = Subgroup.normalClosure ({(ψ u) ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) := by
    rw [Subgroup.map_normalClosure _ _ ψ.surjective]
    simp only [Set.image_singleton, map_pow]
    rfl
  refine ⟨QuotientGroup.congr _ _ ψ hmap, ?_⟩
  change (QuotientGroup.congr (Subgroup.normalClosure ({u ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)))
      (Subgroup.normalClosure ({(ψ u) ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α))) ψ hmap)
      (QuotientGroup.mk u) = QuotientGroup.mk (ψ u)
  rw [QuotientGroup.congr_mk]

/-- **Transport of the Magnus step along a Nielsen transformation.**  The HNN data of a step for the
image `ψ u` — with the norm bound measured against `u` itself, since an automorphism need not
preserve the relator length — transports back to `u`, the root condition being carried by
`nielsenPowerIso`. -/
theorem MagnusStepData.of_aut {α : Type u} {u : FreeGroup α} {l : ℕ}
    (ψ : FreeGroup α ≃* FreeGroup α)
    (h : ∃ (β : Type u) (v : FreeGroup β), ¬ IsProperPower v ∧ relatorNorm v < relatorNorm u ∧
      ∃ (A B : Subgroup (PresentedGroup ({v ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup β)))) (φ : A ≃* B)
        (e : PresentedGroup ({(ψ u) ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) ≃*
          HNNExtension (PresentedGroup ({v ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup β))) A B φ),
        ∃ c : HNNExtension (PresentedGroup ({v ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup β))) A B φ,
          e (PresentedGroup.mk ({(ψ u) ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup α)) (ψ u)) =
            c * HNNExtension.of (PresentedGroup.mk ({v ^ l} : Set (FreeGroup β)) v) * c⁻¹) :
    MagnusStepData u l := by
  obtain ⟨e₁, he₁⟩ := nielsenPowerIso ψ u l
  obtain ⟨β, v, hpp, hlt, A, B, φ, e₂, c, hc⟩ := h
  exact ⟨β, v, hpp, hlt, A, B, φ, e₁.trans e₂, c,
    by rw [MulEquiv.trans_apply, he₁, hc]⟩

/-- **The divisibility hypothesis**, named for reuse: a letter `t` of `u` and a weight `c` with
`c t = 1` killing `u` (equivalently `Σ_x c_x * eps_x u = 0`). -/
def DivisibleRoot {α : Type u} (u : FreeGroup α) : Prop :=
  ∃ (t : α) (c : α → ℤ), t ∈ relatorLetters u ∧ c t = 1 ∧ cohom c u = 1

/-- **The Nielsen route.**  If the divisibility hypothesis `DivisibleRoot` holds at an automorphic
image `ψ u` of `u` whose norm does not exceed that of `u`, then the Magnus step holds for `u`.

This is the proved reduction: the weighted Magnus step `magnusStepCase2_of_weight` at `ψ u` produces
a root of norm `< relatorNorm (ψ u) ≤ relatorNorm u`, and `MagnusStepData.of_aut` transports the
result back along `ψ`. -/
theorem magnusStepData_of_divisible_image {α : Type u} (u : FreeGroup α) (l : ℕ) (hl : 1 ≤ l)
    (_hu : ¬ IsProperPower u) (_hcyc : IsCyclicallyReducedRelator u) (_hn : 2 ≤ relatorNorm u)
    (_hbad : ∀ x : α, x ∈ relatorLetters u → eps x u ≠ 0)
    (ψ : FreeGroup α ≃* FreeGroup α)
    (hpp : ¬ IsProperPower (ψ u)) (hcyc' : IsCyclicallyReducedRelator (ψ u))
    (hn' : 2 ≤ relatorNorm (ψ u)) (hbad' : ∀ x : α, x ∈ relatorLetters (ψ u) → eps x (ψ u) ≠ 0)
    (hdiv : DivisibleRoot (ψ u))
    (hR : relatorNorm (ψ u) ≤ relatorNorm u) :
    MagnusStepData u l := by
  obtain ⟨β, v, hpp', hlt, A, B, φ, e, c, hc⟩ :=
    magnusStepCase2_of_weight (ψ u) l hl hpp hcyc' hn' hbad' hdiv
  exact MagnusStepData.of_aut ψ
    ⟨β, v, hpp', lt_of_lt_of_le hlt hR, A, B, φ, e, c, hc⟩

/-- **The count form of the Nielsen route (the sharp reduction).**  If some automorphic image `ψ u`
of `u` carries a letter `t` and a weight `c` with `c t = 1` killing `ψ u`, and the number of letters
of `ψ u` different from `t` is smaller than `relatorNorm u`, then the Magnus step holds for `u`.

This is strictly sharper than `magnusStepData_of_divisible_image`: the norm of the root produced by
`magnusStepCase2_of_weight_count` is bounded by the *letter count* `#{letters ≠ t}` of `ψ u`, which
may be much smaller than `relatorNorm (ψ u)`.  For `ψ = id` the count condition is automatic
(`#{letters ≠ t} = relatorNorm u - occ_t u < relatorNorm u` whenever `t` occurs), so the content is
then exactly the divisibility condition. -/
theorem magnusStepData_of_count_image {α : Type u} [DecidableEq α] (u : FreeGroup α) (l : ℕ)
    (hl : 1 ≤ l) (_hu : ¬ IsProperPower u) (_hcyc : IsCyclicallyReducedRelator u)
    (_hn : 2 ≤ relatorNorm u) (_hbad : ∀ x : α, x ∈ relatorLetters u → eps x u ≠ 0)
    (ψ : FreeGroup α ≃* FreeGroup α) (t : α) (c : α → ℤ)
    (hpp : ¬ IsProperPower (ψ u)) (hcyc' : IsCyclicallyReducedRelator (ψ u))
    (hn' : 2 ≤ relatorNorm (ψ u)) (hbad' : ∀ x : α, x ∈ relatorLetters (ψ u) → eps x (ψ u) ≠ 0)
    (ht : t ∈ relatorLetters (ψ u)) (hct : c t = 1) (hcu : cohom c (ψ u) = 1)
    (hcount : (wvListAux c t 0 (wordOf (ψ u))).length < relatorNorm u) :
    MagnusStepData u l := by
  obtain ⟨β, v, hpp', hbound, A, B, φ, e, c', hc⟩ :=
    magnusStepCase2_of_weight_count (ψ u) l hl hpp hcyc' hn' hbad' t c ht hct hcu
  exact MagnusStepData.of_aut ψ
    ⟨β, v, hpp', lt_of_le_of_lt hbound hcount, A, B, φ, e, c', hc⟩

/-- **The target from the divisibility case and the residual.**  This is the exact shape of the
remaining gap for `Work.OROneRel.magnus_step_root_no_eps_zero`: the weighted Magnus step
`magnusStepCase2_of_weight` settles every root satisfying the divisibility condition, so the target
follows from the single *residual* statement that it holds for the roots for which no letter
supplies the divisibility condition.  (This is the same reduction as the one at the end of
`Submission/Work/OROneRel/magnus_step_root.lean`, restated here without that file's duplicate
declaration of the target.) -/
theorem magnus_step_root_no_eps_zero_of_residual
    (hres : ∀ {α : Type u} (u : FreeGroup α) (l : ℕ), 1 ≤ l → ¬ IsProperPower u →
      IsCyclicallyReducedRelator u → 2 ≤ relatorNorm u →
      (∀ x : α, x ∈ relatorLetters u → eps x u ≠ 0) → ¬ DivisibleRoot u → MagnusStepData u l)
    {α : Type u} (u : FreeGroup α) (l : ℕ) (hl : 1 ≤ l) (hu : ¬ IsProperPower u)
    (hcyc : IsCyclicallyReducedRelator u) (hn : 2 ≤ relatorNorm u)
    (hbad : ∀ x : α, x ∈ relatorLetters u → eps x u ≠ 0) :
    MagnusStepData u l := by
  by_cases hd : DivisibleRoot u
  · exact magnusStepCase2_of_weight u l hl hu hcyc hn hbad hd
  · exact hres u l hl hu hcyc hn hbad hd

/-- **The residual of the Nielsen route.**  If every automorphic image of `u` of norm `≤ relatorNorm u`
fails the divisibility condition, then the Nielsen route applies to no image of `u`; this is the
precise statement that a future argument (e.g. the `ℤ`-domain / one-relator tower of the
Magnus--Moldavanskii hierarchy) must circumvent. -/
theorem not_divisible_of_residual {α : Type u} (u : FreeGroup α)
    (h : ∀ ψ : FreeGroup α ≃* FreeGroup α, relatorNorm (ψ u) ≤ relatorNorm u →
      ¬ DivisibleRoot (ψ u)) :
    ¬ ∃ ψ : FreeGroup α ≃* FreeGroup α, relatorNorm (ψ u) ≤ relatorNorm u ∧
      DivisibleRoot (ψ u) := by
  rintro ⟨ψ, hR, hd⟩
  exact h ψ hR hd

end Work.OROneRel
